# Messenger project rules

Read `docs/CURSOR-HANDOFF.md` before changing Flutter, deployment, storage, authentication, PWA caching, updates, QR flows, or push notifications.

- Treat `frontend/app` as the active Flutter client.
- Preserve the local-first identity model: never clear IndexedDB/localStorage or server-side-reset a user to fix a client bug.
- Never add `Clear-Site-Data` to production responses.
- Flutter offline service worker stays disabled unless an explicit, tested migration plan is approved.
- Preserve the separately scoped push service worker.
- Every deployed PWA must be built through `frontend/app/scripts/build-web-pwa.sh` so `APP_BUILD_ID` and `deploy-version.json` exist.
- Do not silently force-reload while the user may be composing a message. Detect, notify, then reload on user action.
- Run Dart formatting, Flutter analyze/tests, and a production web build after relevant changes.
- Do not commit secrets, `.env`, private keys, exported identities, or production user data.
